; fault_prefix.kasm -- an over-long prefix chain, and what it reports.
;
; Two things are being compared here, and the second is the reason the program
; exists. The cause is the easy half: a chain longer than seven prefix code
; points is PREFIX_CHAIN_TOO_LONG (spec 3), which the emulator's own tests
; already cover -- its decode loop was once unbounded and this hung it.
;
; The half that needed a program is FAULT_INFO. Every decode fault reports the
; code point it was looking at when it decided, and this fault decides while
; looking at a PREFIX rather than at a main opcode -- so it is the one case
; where "the offending code point" is not the code point that ends the
; instruction. The emulator used to report `ip` here instead, which made this
; one fault report an address where every other decode fault reports a code
; point.
;
; Written as raw `.word`s because there is no mnemonic for a bare prefix: a
; prefix with nothing to prefix is exactly what is being tested.
; expect: FAULT_PREFIX_CHAIN_TOO_LONG

        .org    0

        .word   0x7801          ; XI 1
        .word   0x7801
        .word   0x7801
        .word   0x7801
        .word   0x7801
        .word   0x7801
        .word   0x7801          ; seven: still legal
        .word   0x7801          ; eight: PREFIX_CHAIN_TOO_LONG
        halt
